fetchconfig-web -- Installation
===============================

This guide takes you from an empty web server to a running fetchconfig-web
instance, and covers upgrading an existing installation. It is the operator's
checklist; the full feature reference lives in README.md (rendered as
fetchconfig-web-documentation.html).

fetchconfig-web is a single Perl script (fetchconfig-web.cgi) that sits in front
of an existing fetchconfig (https://github.com/rainer-tammer/fetchconfig)
installation and runs under FastCGI or plain CGI. It needs Perl with a handful
of modules, a PostgreSQL database for its user accounts, a web server that can
run FastCGI or CGI, and read access to fetchconfig's device table and
repository.

